document.paths['/admin/teaching-candidates'].get.description +=
  ' Optional `delivery_mode=in_person|online` makes the appraisal modality-aware. An explicitly incompatible interval warns `unavailable`; a covering legacy/null interval warns `availability_mode_not_declared`. Both remain advisory and never authorize.';

// R117 reconciles the registration boundary after the controlled-UAT journey.
// These replace older bundle-era narratives above rather than appending a
// second contract that leaves both interpretations in the generated document.
document.paths['/registrations'].post.description =
  '**R117 unified registration.** Public and gated by the signed single-use onboarding token; email and Google subject come only from that verified token. Every new applicant supplies Arabic name parts, sex and a valid `phone`; optional French name parts are accepted only as a pair, with an optional nickname. **No generic free-text notes field exists (R121)** — a personal-data field must have a specific documented purpose, and this one had none. `User.phone` remains nullable for honest legacy accounts and no backfill is inferred. An ordinary adult carries her requested `branch_id` and `category_id`. A هيئة التأطير request instead carries strict R115 `framing`, which is planning data and grants nothing. A `parent_child` request carries one or more children, each with her own `requested_branch_id`, `requested_category_id`, identity details and media decision; siblings may differ. Submission atomically creates the Pending guardian, verified identity, request consent, child applications and replay guard. It creates no child User, FamilyLink or child ConsentRecord: each child is independently decided under R62. No Room, Level or Group is accepted. Unknown keys are refused rather than ignored.';
document.paths['/child-applications'].post.description =
  '**R117/R62.** An authenticated adult submits one or more child applications. Each child carries her own required requested Branch and Category, Arabic names, optional French-name pair/nickname, sex, **required full date of birth (R130, `YYYY-MM-DD`)**, optional schooling stage, explicit media decision and the request consent version/instant. Approval materialises the submitted birth date unchanged onto the beneficiary `User` it creates; nothing recomputes it, and no age is ever stored or returned. Submission creates no child User or FamilyLink. Each application is independently approved or rejected; approval materializes the submitted consent and requires exact placement unless an administrator deliberately links an already-placed existing child.';
document.paths['/admin/approvals'].get.description =
  '**R117 approval queue.** Admin or Super Admin only, with TD-12 live-account/role freshness. The union contains registrations, family links, child applications and identity reviews. Registration rows stay compact and carry an explicit `registration_details` projection for the authorized details dialog: submitted applicant names, nickname, sex, phone, verified email and data-processing-consent provenance. Every `children[]` block carries that child\'s submitted identity/schooling details, exact requested Category and Branch, and data/media consent provenance. A mixed family has `branch`/`category` null in the compact row unless every child states the same coordinate; exact child values are never collapsed. `review_user_id` names one applicant and returns at most that still-pending registration review; absent/already-decided/deleted targets return an empty page, never a broader fallback. `type`, `branch_id`, paging and allow-listed sorting remain available when not using exact review; Branch is a reader-selected filter, never authorization scope.';
document.paths['/admin/approvals/{id}/approve'].post.description =
  '**R117 approval semantics.** Adult-beneficiary approval requires complete placement and atomically activates, marks beneficiary, grants structural Student authority and creates the Enrollment(s). A parent/child registration id activates only the guardian: it creates no beneficiary flag, Student assignment or Enrollment for the parent, and leaves every child application for its own independent decision. Staff requests grant only assignments explicitly approved by an authorized caller. Any validation/authorization/notification failure rolls back the whole decision.';
document.paths['/admin/approvals/{id}/reject'].post.description =
  '**R117/R62.** Rejects the exact adult/guardian registration and requires a bounded reason. It does not infer a decision for any child application; each sibling remains independently approvable or rejectable. Rejection and its session/audit effects are one transaction.';
